      \field{abstract}{{PyCoMo} is a python package for quick and easy generation of genome-scale compartmentalized community metabolic models that are compliant with current {openCOBRA} file formats. The resulting models can be used to predict (i) the maximum growth rate at a given abundance profile, (ii) the feasible community compositions at a given growth rate, and (iii) all exchange metabolites and cross-feeding interactions in a community metabolic model independent of the abundance profile; we demonstrate {PyCoMo}’s capability by analysing methane production in a previously published simplified biogas community metabolic model.{PyCoMo} is freely available under an {MIT} licence at http://github.com/{univieCUBE}/{PyCoMo}, the Python Package Index, and Zenodo.}
